{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: implement a `solve(case)` function that filters API calls based on the Toolformer filtering mechanism.\n\nFrom the fixture data and description:\n- Each call has: `call_id`, `loss_without_call`, `loss_with_call`, `prediction_tokens`, `parseable`\n- `threshold`: a float (0.05 in examples)\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. For each call, compute gain = `loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by dividing by `prediction_tokens` (at least 1)\n3. Accept if `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return `accepted_call_ids` and `diagnostics` (in supplied call order)\n\nThe schema says:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: array of strings\n- `diagnostics`: array of objects with `accepted` (bool), `call_id` (string), `normalized_gain` (number)\n\nLet me verify with fixture case 0:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: loss_without=1.48911432, loss_with=0.30132987, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445\n  - normalized_gain = 1.18778445 / 5 = 0.23755689\n  - parseable=true, normalized_gain \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n- call1: 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578, /5 = 0.25375716, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656, /5 = 0.20787531, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153, /3 = 0.39616718, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712, /6 = 0.21730785, parseable=true → accepted\n- call5: 1.98682122 - 0.89260518 = 1.09421604, /4 = 0.27355401, parseable=false → NOT accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call4\"]\n\nThe description says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out the rounding. Probably round to some decimal places. Let me think about what \"rounded\" means here. Maybe just use the computed float value, or round to a certain number of decimal places. The schema just says `\"type\": \"number\"` so any number works. I'll round to 8 decimal places to keep precision but be \"rounded\".\n\nActually, let me re-read: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" This could mean round to some specific number of decimal places. Without more info, I'll round to 8 decimal places (or maybe not round at all and just return the raw float).\n\nActually looking at this more carefully, the values in the fixture are already given to 8 decimal places. I'll compute and round to 8 decimal places for the normalized_gain.\n\nLet me write the solve function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Compute gain\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        \n        # Normalize by prediction tokens (at least 1)\n        n_tokens = max(tokens, 1)\n        normalized_gain = gain / n_tokens\n        \n        # Round\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        \n        # Accept if parseable and normalized gain \u003e= threshold (inclusive)\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain_rounded \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded\n        })\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nNow I need to format this as the required JSON output with `implementation` key containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me format the Python code properly:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = max(call[\"prediction_tokens\"], 1)\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = round(gain / tokens, 8)\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nNow I need to encode this as a JSON string. Let me write it out:\n\nThe response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string value.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = max(call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"], 1)\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = round(gain / tokens, 8)\\n        accepted = bool(parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01XWMJ17BxzyTLKgwcfnvMmE","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2348},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2348,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":34,"output_tokens":1628,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1377},"service_tier":"standard"}}